Butter Chicken Meatballs
  --Lindsay, PinchofYum

1 tbsp avocado oil or olive oil
1/2 onion, roughly chopped
3 cloves garlic, minced (or a garlic paste)
a small piece of fresh ginger, grated (or a ginger paste)
1/4 tsp turmeric
1/4 tsp smoked paprika
1/2 tsp garam masala
1/2 tsp cumin
14 oz can crushed tomatoes or plain tomato sauce
1/2 c water (more as needed later)
1/2 -1 tsp kosher salt
1 tsp sugar
20 oz of cooked chicken or turkey meatballs (~4 c of meatballs)
2 tbsp butter
1/3 c heavy cream (more to taste)
basmati rice (for serving)
cilantro (garnish)

Cook rice. Heat oil over medium heat in a large skillet or Dutch oven over medium heat. Add onion, garlic, ginger, and spices; sauté until softened. Add tomatoes, water, salt, and sugar. Simmer for 10-15 min. Transfer the sauce to a blender and puree until smooth, or use an immersion blender directly in the pot to blend. Add sauce back to the pan. Add the meatballs; simmer with the cover on or keep on low heat until warmed through. Add the butter and cream to make a luscious, heavenly sauce to coat your meatballs. Serve over rice with a sprig or sprinkle of cilantro. Add spiciness to taste with cayenne or chili oil! 

